msgstr ""
"Para este nuevo circuito, la solución ideal podría alcanzarse con todos los "
"parámetros en $0$, lo que confirma que la elección del circuito de "
"referencia es razonable.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now let us compare the number of cost function evaluations, optimizer "
"iterations and time taken with those of the previous attempt.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ahora comparemos el número de evaluaciones de la función de costo, las "
"iteraciones del optimizador y el tiempo empleado con los del intento "
"anterior.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Using our optimal parameters to calculate the minimum eigenvalue:\n"
msgstr ""
"Usando nuestros parámetros óptimos para calcular el valor propio mínimo:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Depending on your specific system, this may or may not result in an "
"improvement in speed or accuracy in this very small scale example. The point"
" is that starting with physically-motivated reference states becomes "
"increasingly important in improving speed and accuracy as problems scale.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dependiendo de tu sistema específico, esto puede o no resultar en una mejora"
" de velocidad o precisión en este ejemplo de escala muy pequeña. Lo "
"importante es que partir de estados de referencia motivados físicamente se "
"vuelve cada vez más relevante para mejorar la velocidad y la precisión a "
"medida que los problemas escalan.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Change the initial point {#change-the-initial-point}"
msgstr "Cambiar el punto inicial {#change-the-initial-point}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now that we have seen the effect of adding the reference state, we will go "
"into what happens when we choose different initial points "
"$\\vec{\\theta_0}$. In particular we will use "
"$\\vec{\\theta_0}=(0,0,0,0,6,0,0,0)$ and "
"$\\vec{\\theta_0}=(6,6,6,6,6,6,6,6,6)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ahora que hemos visto el efecto de agregar el estado de referencia, veamos "
"qué ocurre cuando elegimos distintos puntos iniciales $\\vec{\\theta_0}$. En"
" particular, usaremos $\\vec{\\theta_0}=(0,0,0,0,6,0,0,0)$ y "
"$\\vec{\\theta_0}=(6,6,6,6,6,6,6,6,6)$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Remember that, as discussed when the reference state was introduced, the "
"ideal solution would be found when all the parameters are $0$, so the first "
"initial point should give fewer evaluations.\n"
msgstr ""
"Recuerda que, como se discutió cuando se introdujo el estado de referencia, "
"la solución ideal se encontraría cuando todos los parámetros sean $0$, por "
"lo que el primer punto inicial debería dar menos evaluaciones.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Adjusting initial point to $\\vec{\\theta_0}=(6,6,6,6,6,6,6,6,6)$:\n"
msgstr "Ajustando el punto inicial a $\\vec{\\theta_0}=(6,6,6,6,6,6,6,6,6)$:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"By experimenting with different initial points, you might be able to achieve"
" convergence faster and with fewer function evaluations.\n"
msgstr ""
"Al experimentar con distintos puntos iniciales, es posible que logres una "
"convergencia más rápida y con menos evaluaciones de la función.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Experimenting with different optimizers {#experimenting-with-different-"
"optimizers}"
msgstr ""
"Experimentar con distintos optimizadores {#experimenting-with-different-"
"optimizers}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can adjust the optimizer using SciPy `minimize`'s `method` argument, with"
" more options [found "
"here](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.optimize.minimize.html)."
" We originally used a constrained minimizer (`COBYLA`). In this example, "
"we'll explore using an unconstrained minimizer (`BFGS`) instead\n"
msgstr ""
"Podemos ajustar el optimizador usando el argumento `method` de `minimize` de"
" SciPy, con más opciones [disponibles "
"aquí](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.optimize.minimize.html)."
" Originalmente usamos un minimizador con restricciones (`COBYLA`). En este "
"ejemplo, exploraremos el uso de un minimizador sin restricciones (`BFGS`) en"
" su lugar.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "VQD example {#vqd-example}"
msgstr "Ejemplo de VQD {#vqd-example}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Here we implement the Qiskit patterns framework, explicitly.\n"
msgstr "Aquí implementamos el marco de patrones de Qiskit de forma explícita.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-"
"inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr ""
"Paso 1: Mapear las entradas clásicas a un problema cuántico {#step-1-map-"
"classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now instead of looking for only the lowest eigenvalue of our observables, we"
" will look for all $4$, (where $k=4$).\n"
msgstr ""
"En lugar de buscar solo el autovalor más bajo de nuestros observables, "
"buscaremos los $4$ (donde $k=4$).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Remember that the cost functions of VQD are:\n"
msgstr "Recuerda que las funciones de costo de VQD son:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"C_{l}(\\vec{\\theta}) :=\n"
"\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle +\n"
"\\sum_{j=0}^{l-1}\\beta_j |\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})| \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^j})\\rangle  |^2\n"
"\\quad \\forall l\\in\\{1,\\cdots,k\\}=\\{1,\\cdots,4\\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"C_{l}(\\vec{\\theta}) :=\n"
"\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle +\n"
"\\sum_{j=0}^{l-1}\\beta_j |\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})| \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^j})\\rangle  |^2\n"
"\\quad \\forall l\\in\\{1,\\cdots,k\\}=\\{1,\\cdots,4\\}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is particularly important because a vector "
"$\\vec{\\beta}=(\\beta_0,\\cdots,\\beta_{k-1})$ (in this case $(\\beta_0, "
"\\beta_1, \\beta_2, \\beta_3)$) must be passed as an argument when we define"
" the `VQD` object.\n"
msgstr ""
"Esto es particularmente importante porque un vector "
"$\\vec{\\beta}=(\\beta_0,\\cdots,\\beta_{k-1})$ (en este caso $(\\beta_0, "
"\\beta_1, \\beta_2, \\beta_3)$) debe pasarse como argumento al definir el "
"objeto `VQD`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Also, in Qiskit's implementation of VQD, instead of considering the effective observables described in the previous notebook, the fidelities $|\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})| \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^j})\\rangle  |^2$ are calculated directly via the `ComputeUncompute` algorithm, that leverages a `Sampler` primitive to sample the probability of obtaining $|0\\rangle$ for the circuit\n"
"$U_A^\\dagger(\\vec{\\theta})U_A(\\vec{\\theta^j})$. This works precisely because this probability is\n"
msgstr ""
"Además, en la implementación de VQD de Qiskit, en lugar de considerar los observables efectivos descritos en el cuaderno anterior, las fidelidades $|\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})| \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^j})\\rangle  |^2$ se calculan directamente mediante el algoritmo `ComputeUncompute`, que se apoya en una primitiva `Sampler` para muestrear la probabilidad de obtener $|0\\rangle$ para el circuito\n"
"$U_A^\\dagger(\\vec{\\theta})U_A(\\vec{\\theta^j})$. Esto funciona precisamente porque dicha probabilidad es\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "p_0\n"
msgstr "p_0\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "& = |\\langle 0|U_A^\\dagger(\\vec{\\theta})U_A(\\vec{\\theta^j})|0\\rangle|^2 \\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr ""
"& = |\\langle "
"0|U_A^\\dagger(\\vec{\\theta})U_A(\\vec{\\theta^j})|0\\rangle|^2 \\\\[1mm]\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"& = |\\big(\\langle "
"0|U_A^\\dagger(\\vec{\\theta})\\big)\\big(U_A(\\vec{\\theta^j})|0\\rangle\\big)|^2"
" \\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr ""
"& = |\\big(\\langle "
"0|U_A^\\dagger(\\vec{\\theta})\\big)\\big(U_A(\\vec{\\theta^j})|0\\rangle\\big)|^2"
" \\\\[1mm]\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "& = |\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) |\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^j}) \\rangle|^2 \\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr "& = |\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) |\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^j}) \\rangle|^2 \\\\[1mm]\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-"
"algorithm-design/examples-and-applications/extracted-"
"outputs/e4d59381-43ff-4322-a6f2-df55cef18536-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
